 just rushes back up the roof of the  building using his incredible physical  ability to jump up instantly the man on  the roof looks on in utter shock as  Saitama merely says whew that was close  I saved it up for last I wouldn't want  to drop it the man is so shocked by  saitama's incredible power which seemed  to come out of nowhere that he  accidentally steps off the edge but  Saitama instantly jumps up and saves him  dropping his salmon along the way the  man thanks Saitama and on his way down  he thinks to himself that he didn't have  the courage to jump anyway the man  wonders if he did all that just for  attention if he just wanted someone to  listen to him someone to help him before  he left Saitama told him do what you  want next time you want to jump do it  where I'm eating  we then see a shot of Saitama salmon in  pieces on the ground the man thinks that  Hiro was too good for me as he exits the  building and the people outside take  pictures and videos of him with their  cell phones and some even expressed  disappointment that he didn't jump after  all this fuss as the man walks away from  the crowd thinking about the concept of  just living life the way he wants and  Saitama goes off to fight a monster we  are left with a lot to think about all  that stuff Saitama said at first about  not having an interest in stopping the  man from jumping because he was more  interested in his salmon wasn't true at  all as soon as the man was in genuine  danger  Saitama dropped the salmon without  thinking twice in order to save him this  speaks to the fact that although he  likes to mess around and act like a bit  of a troll at times like so many of us  Millennials saitama's heart is in the  right place he has the heart of a hero  and he will always do the right thing  when it comes down to it also the life  of a traditional salaryman is a  difficult one especially in Japan where  the work hours are extremely long and  the social pressures to fit in and do  well are extremely strong it's easy to  see why this salary man who just lost  everything would feel that he has  nothing to live for and why he would  look down with a version on these young  heroes who receive all this praise just  for walking around in eccentric costumes  this perspective is very similar to how  the older generations look down on  Millennials in our own world they see  Millennials as not working as hard as  they did but the Millennials seem to  need constant praise and adoration  through social media and that's not to  say that social media culture and  celebrity culture don't have serious  problems and one punch man recognizes  that they do the onlookers in this  chapter who seem to actually want to see  the man jump just so they could film it  and probably post it on social media  were representative of a serious problem  and the fact that Saitama is often  accused of being a fraud because people  can't understand that he can be as  strong as he is when he isn't ranked as  high as he should be according to the  hero  Association standards speaks to the fact  that we assigned too much value to  ratings and popularity in our society  including on social media and people are  often misunderstood and even outright  slandered on social media based on  minimal information despite the fact  that Saitama deals with extreme boredom  and lack of purpose because he never  faces any real challenges despite the  fact that he deals with false  accusations and slander and despite the  fact that he starts out as just a hero  for fun Saitama is a true hero whose  heart is in the right place and who  always does the right thing when it  comes down to it as a millennial he  faces unique problems that the older  generation do not fully understand and  they are issues that we can all relate  to what do we do with our lives what is  our purpose how do we cope with the  constant scrutiny gossip and sometimes  outright lies that we all face both in  real life and online like 